  ...toolTexts(TOOL4.chronicleCheck, "Check the chronicle (the files of learned/chronicle/) against the chat as it stands, by code. Each citation is compared with the message at its number: that proves the message exists and reads as cited, not that it supports the line. A line fails where a citation doesn't hold, and where it cites nothing; a line that fails is left out of what the main agent is given. Where a citation's hash is that of exactly one other message, the number was wrong: the check writes the right number into the file itself and says what it corrected. It also lists the stretches of the chat the outline covers nothing of. Run it before you lean on the chronicle, and after you write to it.", { path: "One file of the chronicle, to check that file alone: learned/chronicle/facts.md.", cursor: CURSOR_ARG }),
